      "title": "Setting Headers",
      "lectureOrder": 593,
      "videoOrder": 546,
      "sourceHash": "8cabe59910fb205c60923ec947e59d15f4de8a3c9be23488a79c99b69b4e3035",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 6.33,
          "en": "-: We now kind of enter the second part of this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.33,
          "end": 7.53,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.53,
          "end": 9.36,
          "en": "Thus far we had a thorough look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.36,
          "end": 11.67,
          "en": "at how we can send HTTP requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.67,
          "end": 13.11,
          "en": "how we can handle errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 14.97,
          "en": "how we can work with the data we get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.97,
          "end": 17.91,
          "en": "if we don't have errors and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.91,
          "end": 21.18,
          "en": "Now let me dive into a little bit more advanced parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.18,
          "end": 23.46,
          "en": "of the Angular HTTPClient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.46,
          "end": 25.77,
          "en": "and how you can configure your requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.77,
          "end": 27.72,
          "en": "and which kind of different responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.72,
          "end": 29.91,
          "en": "you can back and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.91,
          "end": 32.22,
          "en": "Let's start with headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.22,
          "end": 34.11,
          "en": "When sending an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.11,
          "end": 36.21,
          "en": "and of course we are configuring our requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 36.21,
          "end": 37.44,
          "en": "in the posts service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 37.44,
          "end": 39.48,
          "en": "So this is the place to look at now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 39.48,
          "end": 42.42,
          "en": "So when configuring these HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 45.93,
          "en": "you set things like the URL you sent the request to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 45.93,
          "end": 47.76,
          "en": "or in the case of a POST request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 47.76,
          "end": 52.76,
          "en": "you also set the data you wanna attach to your request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 52.77,
          "end": 54.51,
          "en": "Now of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 54.51,
          "end": 58.08,
          "en": "sometimes you also need to set some special headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 58.08,
          "end": 58.95,
          "en": "For example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 61.83,
          "en": "when you have a backend that requires authorization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 61.83,
          "end": 64.26,
          "en": "and looks for an authorization header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 64.26,
          "end": 67.02,
          "en": "or if you wanna set your own content type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 67.02,
          "end": 69.27,
          "en": "or you need to attach a custom header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 69.27,
          "end": 73.11,
          "en": "because your API you are sending the request to needs it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 73.11,
          "end": 76.74,
          "en": "Now, setting your own headers is extremely simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 79.41,
          "en": "Any HTTP request method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 79.41,
          "end": 82.17,
          "en": "no matter if it's POST or GET or DELETE",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82.17,
          "end": 83.61,
          "en": "or PATCH or whatever,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 83.61,
          "end": 88.47,
          "en": "any of these methods has an extra last argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.47,
          "end": 90.69,
          "en": "So in the case of GET, it's the second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 90.69,
          "end": 93.3,
          "en": "In the case of POST it would be the third argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 93.3,
          "end": 96.36,
          "en": "which is an object where you can configure that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 96.36,
          "end": 99.39,
          "en": "And there you can configure a bunch of stuff as you can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 99.39,
          "end": 101.58,
          "en": "and will start with the headers here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 101.58,
          "end": 105.09,
          "en": "And headers now takes a header's object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 105.09,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "which allows you to set the headers you wanna send.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 108,
          "end": 111.50999999999999,
          "en": "To be precise, it's a HTTP header's object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 111.50999999999999,
          "end": 116.13,
          "en": "which you need to import from @angular/common/http.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.13,
          "end": 118.89,
          "en": "So you need to add this import at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.89,
          "end": 122.94,
          "en": "And this allows you to create a new instance of this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 122.94,
          "end": 126.36,
          "en": "with a new keyword and queue this object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126.36,
          "end": 128.52,
          "en": "You can pass a JavaScript object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 128.52,
          "end": 130.77,
          "en": "with the object literal notation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.77,
          "end": 134.01,
          "en": "where you can have key value pairs of your headers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.01,
          "end": 137.46,
          "en": "and headers are of course key value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 137.46,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "So for example, here you could set your custom header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 140.49,
          "end": 144.78,
          "en": "in case your API would need that to \"Hello\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 144.78,
          "end": 145.71,
          "en": "or whatever you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 145.71,
          "end": 149.46,
          "en": "You can set any header, any HTTP header pair here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 149.46,
          "end": 152.31,
          "en": "And if I do this and I save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 152.31,
          "end": 154.9,
          "en": "and I now do try to fetch some POSTs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 155.79,
          "end": 157.98,
          "en": "I fetch POSTs as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157.98,
          "end": 160.32,
          "en": "But if we have a look at the Network tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 160.32,
          "end": 163.29,
          "en": "let's actually do that again with the cleared Network tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.29,
          "end": 166.05,
          "en": "and we have a look at our request here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 166.05,
          "end": 168.13,
          "en": "if we inspect the headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 170.31,
          "end": 171.84,
          "en": "you see here on the request headers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.84,
          "end": 174.32999999999998,
          "en": "there is this Custom Header: Hello",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 174.32999999999998,
          "end": 176.37,
          "en": "and that's that custom header I attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 176.37,
          "end": 178.2,
          "en": "and it's as simple as that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 178.2,
          "end": 180.78,
          "en": "You can add as many headers as you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 180.78,
          "end": 182.67,
          "en": "with this simple approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 182.67,
          "end": 186.57,
          "en": "by simply setting the header's conflict option here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 186.57,
          "end": 191.5,
          "en": "to a new HttpHeaders object to which you pass your headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 192.63,
          "end": 195.903,
          "en": "in a object literal with a key value notation.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
